WEBVTT

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:06.294
Captain's Log, Stardate 42523.7.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.772
We are en route

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:11.470
to the newly established
Starbase 173 for port call.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.479
Crew rotation is scheduled

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.414
and we will be off-loading
experiment modules.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.711
Hold it.
That's my chair.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.514
My luck is always lousy

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.487
unless I start
on the dealer's right.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.990
That would seem to be
superstition.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:29.985
Bitter experience has taught me
it's a fundamental truth.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.658
Okay. The game is five-card
stud, nothing wild.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.666
Ante up.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.429
This game is exceedingly simple.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.698
With only 52 cards,
21 of which I will see

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.897
and four other players

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.702
there are a limited number
of winning combinations.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.175
There's more to this
than just the cards, Data.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.336
Of course.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.539
The bets will indicate the
relative strength of each hand.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.105
Time to pluck a pigeon.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.242
Five.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.016
I'm in.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.987
I, too.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.651
Mm-hmm.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.284
I call.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.625
A seven and a six.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.153
Ladies.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.468
I bet ten.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.060
I'll see that.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.504
Call.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.838
Fold.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.967
Yeah, me, too.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.204
I'm out.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.180
I bet five.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.750
I'll see it.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.989
Your five and five.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.525
Too rich for me.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.130
No help.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.470
I bet ten.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.846
Your ten and ten.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.093
Is that what is known
as a poker face?

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.157
Are you playing or not?

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.903
I fold.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.343
You had nothing.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.348
He bluffed you, Data.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.977
It makes very little sense
to bet when you cannot win.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:33.986
But I did win.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.851
I was betting
that you wouldn't call.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.117
How could you tell?

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.387
Instinct, Data.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.722
Instinct.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.457
The game is seven-card high/low
with a buy on the last card.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.692
And just to make it
more interesting

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.667
the man with the ax takes all.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.982
My god.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.966
Phillipa Louvois

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.468
and back in uniform.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.629
It's been ten years

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.468
but seeing you again like this

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.974
makes it seem like 50.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.635
If we weren't around
all these people

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.304
do you know what
I would like to do?

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.972
Bust a chair across my teeth?

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:34.980
After that.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.005
Oh, ain't love wonderful?

00:03:56.736 --> 00:04:01.139
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:04.939
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.944
Its continuing mission--

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:10.948
to explore strange new worlds

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:15.454
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:19.982
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:24.553
So, what are you doing out here?

00:05:24.589 --> 00:05:27.581
I am in charge
of the 23rd Sector JAG Office.

00:05:27.626 --> 00:05:28.718
We're brand new.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.888
I have no staff,
but one terrified little Ensign.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.058
And, hopefully, we can make
some good law out here.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.125
Anything is possible.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.603
So you came back to Starfleet.

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.902
Still the most
worthwhile place to be.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.567
You had no reason to leave.

00:05:43.608 --> 00:05:44.768
They forced me out.

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:49.973
No, that was your own
damn stubborn pride.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.983
When I prosecuted you
in the Stargazer court-martial

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:54.450
I was doing my job.

00:05:54.486 --> 00:05:55.783
Oh, you did more than your job.

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:56.788
You enjoyed it.

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:57.914
Not true.

00:05:57.956 --> 00:05:59.821
A court-martial
is standard procedure

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:00.916
when a ship is lost.

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:01.926
I was doing my duty

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.258
as an officer of the Judge
Advocate General.

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:08.255
You always enjoyed
the adversarial process

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.996
more than getting at the truth.

00:06:12.904 --> 00:06:17.773
Well, I hope that you've learned
a little wisdom along the way.

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:24.107
You know, I never thought
I would say this

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:26.845
but it's good to see you again.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:31.652
It brings a sense of order
and stability to my universe

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:35.148
to know that you're still
a pompous ass.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.390
And a damn sexy man.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:44.061
Captain Picard?

00:06:45.036 --> 00:06:46.162
Admiral.

00:06:46.204 --> 00:06:47.171
Captain Louvois.

00:06:47.205 --> 00:06:48.968
You're acquainted
with Captain Picard?

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.098
Oh, yes.

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.872
We're old... friends.

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:54.276
Excuse me.

00:06:54.312 --> 00:06:56.507
Picard, call me.

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:59.449
You can buy me dinner.

00:06:59.484 --> 00:07:01.748
Captain, it's good
to see you again.

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:02.845
Admiral.

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.753
May I present
Commander Bruce Maddox.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:05.757
Commander.

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.224
He has an interesting

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.659
proposal for you,
but that can wait for awhile.

00:07:09.694 --> 00:07:11.889
I'm eager to see the Enterprise.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.830
Yes, sir.
This way.

00:07:22.507 --> 00:07:24.975
Admiral on the Bridge.

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:29.947
I was a little surprised
at the decision

00:07:29.981 --> 00:07:31.073
to put a base in force

00:07:31.116 --> 00:07:33.277
so close to the Neutral Zone.

00:07:33.318 --> 00:07:34.945
As you know, we've
had disturbing news

00:07:35.053 --> 00:07:36.577
from both sides of the zone.

00:07:36.621 --> 00:07:39.556
We're here to respond
when needed.

00:07:39.591 --> 00:07:41.684
And it won't hurt
to have the Romulans know

00:07:41.726 --> 00:07:44.957
that we're nearby.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:48.431
Ah. Well, Captain, I want to
thank you for this opportunity.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:49.695
For 500 years, every ship

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.702
that has born the name
of the Enterprise

00:07:51.736 --> 00:07:52.725
has become a legend.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:53.965
This one is no different.

00:07:54.072 --> 00:07:55.334
Admiral.

00:07:55.373 --> 00:07:56.567
Oh, yes.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:08:00.339
Captain, Commander Maddox is
here to work on your android.

00:08:00.378 --> 00:08:01.970
Please take care of him.

00:08:06.985 --> 00:08:08.919
How have you been, Data?

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:10.785
My condition does not alter

00:08:10.822 --> 00:08:13.222
with the passage of time,
Commander.

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:14.555
Are the two of you acquainted?

00:08:14.593 --> 00:08:16.117
Yes, I evaluated Data

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:18.823
when it first applied
to the academy.

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:22.027
And was the sole member of the
committee to oppose my entrance

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:24.467
on the grounds
that I was not a sentient being.

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:28.166
What exactly will this work
entail?

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:33.239
I am going to disassemble Data.

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:39.005
All right,
explain this procedure.

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:43.450
Ever since I first saw Data
at the entrance evaluation

00:08:43.488 --> 00:08:44.921
at the Starfleet Academy

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:46.753
I've wanted to understand it.

00:08:46.791 --> 00:08:48.281
I became a student of the works

00:08:48.326 --> 00:08:51.523
of Dr. Noonien Soong,
Data's creator

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:54.293
and I've tried
to continue his work.

00:08:54.332 --> 00:08:58.098
I believe I am very close
to the breakthrough

00:08:58.136 --> 00:09:02.300
that will enable me
to duplicate Dr. Soong's work

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.001
and replicate this.

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:08.170
But, as a first step

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:11.273
I must disassemble and study it.

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:14.183
Data is going to be my guide.

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:16.784
Data?

00:09:16.821 --> 00:09:20.120
It sounds intriguing.

00:09:20.158 --> 00:09:21.682
How will you proceed?

00:09:21.726 --> 00:09:23.751
I will run a full diagnostic
on Data

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:26.457
evaluating the condition
of its current software.

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:28.295
I will then dump its core memory

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.301
into the Starbase
mainframe computer

00:09:30.335 --> 00:09:33.498
and begin a detailed analysis
of its construction.

00:09:33.538 --> 00:09:36.234
You've constructed
a positronic brain?

00:09:36.274 --> 00:09:37.866
Yes.

00:09:37.909 --> 00:09:40.901
Have you determined
how the electron resistance

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:43.915
across the neural filaments
is to be resolved?

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.974
Not precisely.

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:51.249
That would seem to be
a necessary first step.

00:09:51.289 --> 00:09:54.656
I am confident
that I will find the answer

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:57.321
once I examine
the filament links

00:09:57.362 --> 00:09:59.353
in your anterior cortex.

00:09:59.397 --> 00:10:02.423
But, if the answer
is not forthcoming

00:10:02.467 --> 00:10:05.493
your model will not function.

00:10:05.537 --> 00:10:08.700
I do not anticipate
any problems.

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:11.174
You seem a little vague
on the specifics.

00:10:11.209 --> 00:10:14.975
What are the risks
to Commander Data?

00:10:15.046 --> 00:10:17.139
Negligible.

00:10:17.182 --> 00:10:18.672
Captain

00:10:18.717 --> 00:10:22.813
I believe his basic research
lacks the specifics necessary

00:10:22.854 --> 00:10:25.982
to support an experiment
of this magnitude.

00:10:26.057 --> 00:10:29.993
Commander Data is a valued
member of my Bridge crew.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:34.327
Based on what I've heard,
I cannot allow Commander Data

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:37.199
to submit himself
to this experiment.

00:10:37.235 --> 00:10:40.727
I was afraid this might be
your attitude, Captain.

00:10:40.772 --> 00:10:43.297
Here are Starfleet's
transfer orders

00:10:43.341 --> 00:10:45.571
separating Commander Data
from the Enterprise

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.942
and reassigning it
to Starbase 173

00:10:47.979 --> 00:10:49.947
under my command.

00:10:49.981 --> 00:10:53.712
Data, I will see you
in my office tomorrow

00:10:53.752 --> 00:10:55.049
at 0900 hours.

00:11:17.141 --> 00:11:19.132
Come.

00:11:20.978 --> 00:11:23.105
You sent for me, sir?

00:11:23.147 --> 00:11:25.479
Data, please sit down.

00:11:29.153 --> 00:11:31.451
Well, we have a problem.

00:11:31.489 --> 00:11:33.923
I find myself
in complete agreement

00:11:33.958 --> 00:11:37.052
with that assessment
of the situation, sir.

00:11:38.996 --> 00:11:42.625
Your service to this ship
has been exemplary.

00:11:42.667 --> 00:11:44.862
I don't want to lose you.

00:11:44.902 --> 00:11:49.396
I will not submit
to the procedure, sir.

00:11:52.109 --> 00:11:54.100
Data...

00:11:56.447 --> 00:11:59.416
I understand your objections

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:03.409
but I have to consider
Starfleet's interests.

00:12:03.454 --> 00:12:06.252
What if Commander Maddox
is correct?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.087
There is a possibility

00:12:08.125 --> 00:12:11.094
that many more beings
like yourself

00:12:11.128 --> 00:12:12.857
can be constructed.

00:12:12.897 --> 00:12:17.596
Sir, Lieutenant La Forge's eyes
are far superior

00:12:17.635 --> 00:12:20.604
to human
biological eyes, true?

00:12:20.638 --> 00:12:22.105
Mm-hmm.

00:12:22.139 --> 00:12:25.768
Then why are not all
human officers required

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:29.576
to have their eyes replaced
with cybernetic implants?

00:12:35.987 --> 00:12:37.284
I see.

00:12:37.321 --> 00:12:41.314
It is precisely because
I am not human.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:45.486
That will be all, Mr. Data.

00:12:55.106 --> 00:12:58.234
Computer, pull
all relevant information

00:12:58.275 --> 00:13:01.244
with regard
to Starfleet regulations

00:13:01.278 --> 00:13:03.576
on the transfer of officers.

00:13:03.614 --> 00:13:05.844
Working.

00:13:13.557 --> 00:13:14.751
My god.

00:13:14.792 --> 00:13:16.953
Twice in as many days.

00:13:16.994 --> 00:13:18.427
I need your help.

00:13:18.462 --> 00:13:20.521
An historic moment.

00:13:20.564 --> 00:13:24.261
I have been trying to make sense
of this gobbledygook

00:13:24.301 --> 00:13:25.928
but it's beyond me.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.494
The fact is,
my android officer, Data

00:13:27.538 --> 00:13:29.733
is being transferred
compulsorily

00:13:29.774 --> 00:13:31.639
to be made part
of a highly dangerous

00:13:31.675 --> 00:13:34.371
and ill-conceived experiment,
and I want it stopped.

00:13:34.412 --> 00:13:37.973
He can refuse
to undergo the procedure

00:13:38.049 --> 00:13:40.449
but we can't stop the transfer.

00:13:40.484 --> 00:13:44.113
Once this Maddox
has got control of Data

00:13:44.155 --> 00:13:46.123
anything could happen.

00:13:46.157 --> 00:13:48.387
I don't trust that man.

00:13:48.426 --> 00:13:51.520
We agree to certain risks
when we join Starfleet.

00:13:51.562 --> 00:13:53.723
Yes, acceptable risks,
justified risks

00:13:53.764 --> 00:13:55.163
but I can't accept this.

00:13:55.199 --> 00:13:56.894
It's unjustified.
It's unfair.

00:13:56.934 --> 00:13:57.901
He has rights.

00:13:57.935 --> 00:14:01.371
All this passion over a machine?

00:14:01.405 --> 00:14:02.929
Don't start.

00:14:02.973 --> 00:14:05.464
This is important to me.

00:14:06.777 --> 00:14:08.836
Is there an option?

00:14:08.879 --> 00:14:11.746
There is always an option.

00:14:11.782 --> 00:14:13.477
He can resign.

00:14:16.954 --> 00:14:18.785
I see.

00:14:18.823 --> 00:14:21.417
So you came to me for help.

00:14:21.459 --> 00:14:22.858
Yes, I came to you.

00:14:22.893 --> 00:14:25.726
You're the JAG Officer
for this sector.

00:14:25.763 --> 00:14:28.323
I had no choice
but to come to you.

00:14:28.365 --> 00:14:30.265
Wait.

00:14:32.303 --> 00:14:34.931
I didn't mean it that way.

00:14:34.972 --> 00:14:38.100
I'm glad you felt you could...

00:14:38.142 --> 00:14:39.837
well, come to me.

00:14:39.877 --> 00:14:42.971
The word "trust" just isn't
in your vocabulary, is it?

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:45.412
Good try--
nine out of ten for effort.

00:14:45.449 --> 00:14:47.610
I wish things were different.

00:14:47.651 --> 00:14:50.814
I wish I could believe that.

00:16:08.199 --> 00:16:12.568
"When in disgrace
with fortune and men's eyes

00:16:12.603 --> 00:16:16.562
I all alone beweep
my outcast state."

00:16:16.607 --> 00:16:18.905
Is it just words to you?

00:16:18.943 --> 00:16:21.776
Or do you fathom the meaning?

00:16:21.812 --> 00:16:24.337
Is it not customary
to request permission

00:16:24.381 --> 00:16:26.941
before entering
an individual's quarters?

00:16:26.984 --> 00:16:30.317
I thought that we
could talk this out.

00:16:30.354 --> 00:16:33.221
That I could try
to persuade you.

00:16:33.257 --> 00:16:37.421
Your memories and knowledge
will remain intact.

00:16:37.461 --> 00:16:40.328
Reduced to the mere
facts of the events.

00:16:40.364 --> 00:16:44.266
The substance, the flavor
of the moment could be lost.

00:16:44.301 --> 00:16:45.962
Take games of chance...

00:16:46.036 --> 00:16:47.435
Games of chance?

00:16:47.471 --> 00:16:49.439
Yes, I had read and absorbed

00:16:49.473 --> 00:16:52.533
every treatise and textbook
on the subject

00:16:52.576 --> 00:16:56.535
and found myself well prepared
for the experience.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.980
Yet, when I finally
played poker

00:16:59.083 --> 00:17:01.381
I discovered that the reality

00:17:01.418 --> 00:17:04.387
bore little resemblance
to the rules.

00:17:04.421 --> 00:17:06.048
And the point being?

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:07.921
That, while I believe
it is possible

00:17:08.025 --> 00:17:10.926
to download information
contained in a positronic brain

00:17:11.028 --> 00:17:14.191
I do not believe you have
acquired the expertise necessary

00:17:14.231 --> 00:17:18.258
to preserve the essence
of those experiences.

00:17:18.302 --> 00:17:20.862
There is an ineffable quality
to memory

00:17:20.904 --> 00:17:24.237
which I do not believe
can survive your procedure.

00:17:24.275 --> 00:17:27.108
"lneffable quality."

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.579
I had rather we had
done this together

00:17:32.616 --> 00:17:36.245
but, one way or the other,
we are doing it.

00:17:36.287 --> 00:17:38.346
You're under my command.

00:17:38.389 --> 00:17:39.754
No, sir.

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:43.248
I am not under yours
nor anyone else's command.

00:17:43.294 --> 00:17:45.762
I have resigned from Starfleet.

00:17:45.796 --> 00:17:46.956
Resigned?

00:17:46.997 --> 00:17:49.625
You can't resign.

00:17:49.667 --> 00:17:52.693
I regret the decision,
but I must.

00:17:52.736 --> 00:17:56.536
I am the culmination
of one man's dream.

00:17:56.573 --> 00:18:01.909
This is not ego or vanity,
but when Dr. Soong created me

00:18:01.945 --> 00:18:04.880
he added to the substance
of the universe.

00:18:04.915 --> 00:18:07.713
If, by your experiments,
I am destroyed

00:18:07.751 --> 00:18:11.209
something unique, something
wonderful will be lost.

00:18:11.255 --> 00:18:13.280
I cannot permit that.

00:18:13.324 --> 00:18:16.384
I must protect his dream.

00:18:16.427 --> 00:18:18.520
And so must l.

00:18:18.562 --> 00:18:19.722
But keep packing

00:18:19.763 --> 00:18:21.560
because, one way or the other

00:18:21.598 --> 00:18:23.930
you will be reporting.

00:18:34.011 --> 00:18:35.444
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:18:35.479 --> 00:18:37.743
Commander Bruce Maddox,
having been thwarted

00:18:37.781 --> 00:18:39.248
by Data's abrupt resignation

00:18:39.283 --> 00:18:41.513
is now seeking
a legal remedy for his woes.

00:18:41.552 --> 00:18:43.713
Captain Louvois
has requested my presence

00:18:43.754 --> 00:18:44.914
at those discussions.

00:18:44.955 --> 00:18:47.617
Your response is
emotional and irrational.

00:18:47.658 --> 00:18:48.682
Irrational?

00:18:48.726 --> 00:18:51.854
You are endowing Data
with human characteristics

00:18:51.895 --> 00:18:54.363
because it looks human,
but it is not.

00:18:54.398 --> 00:18:55.956
If it were a box on wheels

00:18:56.066 --> 00:18:58.466
I would not be facing
this opposition.

00:18:58.502 --> 00:19:02.029
Overt sentimentality is not one
of Captain Picard's failings.

00:19:02.072 --> 00:19:03.505
Trust me, I know.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:05.201
I will tell you again.

00:19:05.242 --> 00:19:08.040
Data is a valued
member of my crew.

00:19:08.078 --> 00:19:10.911
He's an outstanding
Bridge Officer.

00:19:10.981 --> 00:19:14.314
If I am permitted to make
this experiment, the horizons

00:19:14.351 --> 00:19:17.047
for human achievement
become boundless.

00:19:17.087 --> 00:19:20.716
Consider, every ship in
Starfleet with a Data on board.

00:19:20.758 --> 00:19:24.216
Utilizing it's
extraordinary capabilities

00:19:24.261 --> 00:19:28.322
acting as our hands and eyes
in dangerous situations.

00:19:28.365 --> 00:19:30.196
Look, you're preaching
to the choir, here.

00:19:30.234 --> 00:19:31.633
Why don't you get to the point?

00:19:31.668 --> 00:19:34.228
Data must not be
permitted to resign.

00:19:34.271 --> 00:19:35.829
Data is a Starfleet Officer.

00:19:35.873 --> 00:19:37.431
He still has certain rights.

00:19:37.474 --> 00:19:38.600
Right, rights!

00:19:38.642 --> 00:19:40.803
I'm sick to death
of hearing about rights.

00:19:40.844 --> 00:19:43.108
What about my right
not to have my life work

00:19:43.147 --> 00:19:44.637
subverted
by blind ignorance?

00:19:44.681 --> 00:19:45.670
We have rule of law

00:19:45.716 --> 00:19:46.683
in this Federation.

00:19:46.717 --> 00:19:47.945
You cannot simply
seize people

00:19:48.052 --> 00:19:50.452
and experiment with them
to prove your pet theories.

00:19:50.487 --> 00:19:51.454
Thank you.

00:19:51.488 --> 00:19:52.785
Now you're doing it.

00:19:52.823 --> 00:19:55.417
Data is an extraordinary
piece of engineering

00:19:55.459 --> 00:19:57.086
but it is a machine.

00:19:57.127 --> 00:19:58.788
If you permit it to resign

00:19:58.829 --> 00:20:01.525
it will destroy years
of work in robotics.

00:20:01.565 --> 00:20:04.864
Starfleet does not have
to allow the resignation.

00:20:04.902 --> 00:20:07.393
Commander, who do you think
you're working for?

00:20:07.438 --> 00:20:09.838
Starfleet is not an organization
that ignores

00:20:09.873 --> 00:20:12.569
it's own regulations
when they become inconvenient.

00:20:12.609 --> 00:20:15.305
Whether you like it or not,
Data does have rights.

00:20:15.345 --> 00:20:18.109
Let me put it another way.

00:20:18.148 --> 00:20:22.448
Would you permit the computer
of the Enterprise

00:20:22.486 --> 00:20:24.784
to refuse a refit?

00:20:24.822 --> 00:20:26.881
That's an interesting point.

00:20:26.924 --> 00:20:29.825
But the Enterprise computer
is property.

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:30.827
Is Data?

00:20:30.861 --> 00:20:31.919
Of course.

00:20:31.962 --> 00:20:35.090
There may be law
to support this position.

00:20:35.132 --> 00:20:36.099
Then find it.

00:20:36.133 --> 00:20:39.500
A ruling with such
broad-ranging implications

00:20:39.536 --> 00:20:40.901
must be supported.

00:20:40.938 --> 00:20:42.269
Phillipa

00:20:42.306 --> 00:20:44.797
I hope you will use
the same zeal

00:20:44.842 --> 00:20:48.471
that you did in
the Stargazer court-martial.

00:20:56.954 --> 00:21:01.254
Data, you're supposed
to rip the wrapping off.

00:21:01.291 --> 00:21:05.421
With the application
of a little care, Wes

00:21:05.462 --> 00:21:08.431
the paper can be
utilized again.

00:21:08.465 --> 00:21:10.956
Data, you're missing
the point.

00:21:16.473 --> 00:21:19.772
The Dream of the Fire
by K'Ratak.

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:21.437
Thank you, Worf.

00:21:21.478 --> 00:21:23.343
It was in the hands
of the Klingons

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.610
that the novel attained
its full stature.

00:21:25.649 --> 00:21:26.980
I couldn't disagree more

00:21:27.017 --> 00:21:28.609
but we'll save that argument

00:21:28.652 --> 00:21:29.880
for another day.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.785
Excuse me, please.

00:21:33.657 --> 00:21:35.625
Is something wrong?

00:21:37.494 --> 00:21:39.462
Of course there is.

00:21:39.496 --> 00:21:41.464
You're going away.

00:21:41.498 --> 00:21:44.831
No one regrets that necessity
more than myself

00:21:44.868 --> 00:21:47.234
but you do understand
my reasons?

00:21:47.271 --> 00:21:48.738
Sure, I understand.

00:21:48.772 --> 00:21:51.900
I just don't like
you being forced out.

00:21:51.942 --> 00:21:53.170
It's not fair.

00:21:55.779 --> 00:21:59.840
As Dr. Pulaski would, at this
junction, no doubt remind us

00:21:59.883 --> 00:22:01.441
"life is rarely fair."

00:22:01.485 --> 00:22:05.421
Sorry, that just doesn't
make it any better.

00:22:05.455 --> 00:22:09.789
I shall miss you, Geordi.

00:22:09.826 --> 00:22:11.919
Yeah.

00:22:11.962 --> 00:22:14.123
Me, too.

00:22:16.633 --> 00:22:19.898
Take care of yourself, Data.

00:22:25.509 --> 00:22:27.443
I have completed my research.

00:22:27.477 --> 00:22:32.414
Based on the Acts of Cumberland
passed in the early 21st century

00:22:32.449 --> 00:22:35.441
Data is the property
of Starfleet.

00:22:35.485 --> 00:22:38.784
He cannot resign
and he cannot refuse

00:22:38.822 --> 00:22:41.791
to cooperate
with Commander Maddox.

00:22:41.825 --> 00:22:44.316
What if I challenge
this ruling?

00:22:44.361 --> 00:22:47.159
Then I shall be required
to hold a hearing.

00:22:47.197 --> 00:22:48.289
Then I so challenge.

00:22:48.332 --> 00:22:49.492
Convene your hearing.

00:22:49.533 --> 00:22:52.001
Captain, that would be
exceedingly difficult.

00:22:52.069 --> 00:22:53.559
This is a new base.

00:22:53.604 --> 00:22:54.730
I have no staff.

00:22:54.771 --> 00:22:57.638
Surely, Captain,
you have regulations

00:22:57.674 --> 00:23:00.507
to take care
of such an eventuality.

00:23:00.544 --> 00:23:01.602
There are.

00:23:01.645 --> 00:23:04.773
I can use serving officers
as legal counsel.

00:23:04.815 --> 00:23:07.750
You, as the senior officer,
would defend.

00:23:07.784 --> 00:23:10.344
Very good.

00:23:10.387 --> 00:23:13.117
And the unenviable task
of prosecuting this case

00:23:13.156 --> 00:23:14.783
would fall on you, Commander

00:23:14.825 --> 00:23:17.851
as the next most senior officer
of the defendant's ship.

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:20.597
I can't.

00:23:20.631 --> 00:23:21.598
I won't.

00:23:21.632 --> 00:23:22.894
Data's my comrade.

00:23:22.933 --> 00:23:24.662
We have served together.

00:23:24.701 --> 00:23:28.193
I not only respect him,
I consider him my friend.

00:23:28.238 --> 00:23:31.696
When people of good conscience
have an honest dispute

00:23:31.742 --> 00:23:33.733
we must still sometimes resort

00:23:33.777 --> 00:23:36.075
to this kind
of adversarial system.

00:23:36.113 --> 00:23:38.980
You just want me to prove
that Data is a mere machine.

00:23:39.016 --> 00:23:41.314
I can't do that,
because I don't believe it.

00:23:41.351 --> 00:23:42.579
I happen to know better

00:23:42.619 --> 00:23:43.950
so I am neither qualified

00:23:43.987 --> 00:23:44.954
nor willing.

00:23:44.988 --> 00:23:47.320
You're going to have
to find someone else.

00:23:47.357 --> 00:23:50.087
Then I will rule summarily
based on my findings.

00:23:50.127 --> 00:23:51.219
Data is a toaster.

00:23:51.261 --> 00:23:54.162
Have him report immediately
to Commander Maddox

00:23:54.197 --> 00:23:55.664
for experimental refit.

00:24:00.437 --> 00:24:01.563
I see.

00:24:01.605 --> 00:24:04.665
I have no choice but to agree.

00:24:04.708 --> 00:24:07.836
Good, and I expect you to do
your duty in that courtroom.

00:24:07.878 --> 00:24:09.209
If I find for one minute

00:24:09.246 --> 00:24:11.043
that you are not doing your best

00:24:11.081 --> 00:24:12.946
I will end this, then and there.

00:24:14.484 --> 00:24:17.453
You don't have to remind us
of our duty.

00:24:21.792 --> 00:24:23.919
You just...

00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:26.451
just remember yours.

00:24:26.496 --> 00:24:28.896
I have never forgotten it.

00:24:28.932 --> 00:24:32.231
Not then, and certainly not now.

00:24:45.115 --> 00:24:46.446
Come.

00:24:48.218 --> 00:24:49.651
Data

00:24:49.686 --> 00:24:51.950
Captain Louvois
has issued a ruling.

00:24:51.989 --> 00:24:54.981
You are the property
of Starfleet Command.

00:24:55.059 --> 00:24:56.424
You cannot resign.

00:24:57.428 --> 00:24:58.395
I see.

00:24:58.429 --> 00:24:59.760
From limitless options

00:24:59.797 --> 00:25:01.924
I am reduced to none,
or rather one.

00:25:01.999 --> 00:25:04.229
I can only hope
that Commander Maddox

00:25:04.268 --> 00:25:06.532
is more capable
than it would appear.

00:25:06.570 --> 00:25:08.538
Data, you're not
going to submit.

00:25:08.572 --> 00:25:10.130
We are going to fight this.

00:25:10.174 --> 00:25:12.039
I've challenged the ruling.

00:25:12.076 --> 00:25:14.943
Captain Louvois will be
compelled to convene a hearing.

00:25:14.978 --> 00:25:18.470
She may be overly attached
to the letter of the law

00:25:18.515 --> 00:25:21.382
but I suspect that she still
understands its spirit.

00:25:21.418 --> 00:25:22.442
We will put to rest

00:25:22.486 --> 00:25:25.080
this question of your legal
status once and for all.

00:25:25.122 --> 00:25:27.090
Now, I have been asked
to represent you

00:25:27.124 --> 00:25:28.751
but if there is
some other officer

00:25:28.792 --> 00:25:30.692
with which you would feel
more happy...

00:25:30.727 --> 00:25:33.958
Captain, I have complete
confidence in your ability

00:25:33.997 --> 00:25:35.692
to represent my interests.

00:25:48.879 --> 00:25:50.403
Computer

00:25:50.447 --> 00:25:52.574
identify Riker, William T.

00:25:52.616 --> 00:25:56.074
Access code theta alpha
two, seven, three, seven

00:25:56.120 --> 00:25:57.417
blue enable.

00:25:57.454 --> 00:26:00.184
Riker, William T. identified.

00:26:00.224 --> 00:26:01.885
Ready.

00:26:01.925 --> 00:26:05.554
Access all available
technical schematics

00:26:05.596 --> 00:26:08.190
on Lieutenant Commander Data.

00:26:08.232 --> 00:26:09.722
Working.

00:26:36.627 --> 00:26:39.619
This hearing, convened
on Stardate 42527.4

00:26:39.663 --> 00:26:44.123
is to determine the legal status
of the android known as Data.

00:26:44.168 --> 00:26:46.261
The Office
of Judge Advocate General

00:26:46.303 --> 00:26:48.328
has rendered a finding
of property.

00:26:48.372 --> 00:26:49.964
The defense has challenged.

00:26:50.040 --> 00:26:50.972
Commander Riker?

00:26:51.041 --> 00:26:52.906
Your Honor, there
is only one issue

00:26:52.943 --> 00:26:54.843
and one relevant
piece of evidence.

00:26:54.878 --> 00:26:56.709
I call Lieutenant
Commander Data.

00:27:05.255 --> 00:27:08.554
Verify Lieutenant
Commander Data.

00:27:08.592 --> 00:27:12.426
Current assignment:
USS Enterprise.

00:27:12.462 --> 00:27:14.430
Starfleet Command
decoration for...

00:27:14.464 --> 00:27:16.932
Your Honor, we'll
stipulate to all of this.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.332
Objection, Your Honor.

00:27:19.369 --> 00:27:21.200
I want this read.

00:27:21.238 --> 00:27:22.330
All of it.

00:27:22.372 --> 00:27:24.340
Sustained.

00:27:24.374 --> 00:27:28.071
...valor and gallantry,
Medal of Honor with clusters

00:27:28.111 --> 00:27:31.376
Legion of Honor, the Star Cross.

00:27:33.250 --> 00:27:35.480
Proceed, Commander.

00:27:36.720 --> 00:27:39.712
Commander, what are you?

00:27:41.191 --> 00:27:42.283
An android.

00:27:42.326 --> 00:27:44.351
Which is?

00:27:44.394 --> 00:27:47.625
Webster's 24th Century
Dictionary, Fifth Edition

00:27:47.664 --> 00:27:49.962
defines an android
as an automaton

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.093
made to resemble a human being.

00:27:52.135 --> 00:27:53.966
"An automaton."

00:27:54.037 --> 00:27:55.937
Made by whom?

00:27:56.940 --> 00:27:57.907
Sir?

00:27:57.941 --> 00:27:59.636
Who built you, Commander?

00:27:59.676 --> 00:28:01.109
Dr. Noonien Soong.

00:28:01.144 --> 00:28:02.168
And he was?

00:28:02.212 --> 00:28:04.806
The foremost authority
on cybernetics.

00:28:04.848 --> 00:28:06.475
More basic than that.

00:28:06.516 --> 00:28:07.505
What was he?

00:28:10.587 --> 00:28:11.781
Human?

00:28:12.923 --> 00:28:14.220
Thank you.

00:28:15.225 --> 00:28:18.058
Commander, what is the capacity
of your memory

00:28:18.095 --> 00:28:20.563
and how fast can you access
information?

00:28:20.597 --> 00:28:23.430
I have
an ultimate storage capacity

00:28:23.467 --> 00:28:25.492
of 800 quadrillion bits.

00:28:25.535 --> 00:28:28.504
My total linear computational
speed has been rated

00:28:28.538 --> 00:28:31.063
at 60 trillion operations
per second.

00:28:35.245 --> 00:28:37.941
Your Honor, I offer
into evidence

00:28:37.981 --> 00:28:40.040
Prosecution's Exhibit "A."

00:28:40.083 --> 00:28:41.550
A rod of parsteel

00:28:41.585 --> 00:28:44.179
tensile strength 40 kilo-bars.

00:28:48.225 --> 00:28:49.658
Commander, would you bend that?

00:28:49.693 --> 00:28:50.660
Objection.

00:28:50.694 --> 00:28:52.855
There are many
life-forms possessed

00:28:52.896 --> 00:28:53.863
with megastrength.

00:28:53.897 --> 00:28:56.161
These issues are not relevant
to this hearing.

00:28:56.199 --> 00:28:58.099
I'm afraid I can't agree,
Captain.

00:28:58.135 --> 00:29:00.603
Proceed with your demonstration,
Commander.

00:29:17.220 --> 00:29:19.780
Drawing on the log
of the construction

00:29:19.823 --> 00:29:21.848
of the prototype android Lore

00:29:21.892 --> 00:29:24.224
also constructed
by Noonien Soong

00:29:24.261 --> 00:29:25.853
I request to be allowed

00:29:25.896 --> 00:29:27.921
to remove the Commander's hand

00:29:28.031 --> 00:29:29.430
for your inspection.

00:29:29.466 --> 00:29:31.195
Objection.

00:29:34.905 --> 00:29:36.896
It doesn't matter.

00:29:39.242 --> 00:29:41.608
Objection withdrawn.

00:29:44.514 --> 00:29:46.243
Proceed, Commander.

00:29:50.620 --> 00:29:51.985
I'm sorry.

00:30:11.274 --> 00:30:15.768
The Commander is a physical
representation of a dream

00:30:15.812 --> 00:30:19.373
an idea conceived of
by the mind of a man.

00:30:19.416 --> 00:30:23.614
Its purpose-- to serve human
needs and interests.

00:30:23.653 --> 00:30:26.588
It's a collection
of neural nets

00:30:26.623 --> 00:30:28.784
and heuristic algorithms.

00:30:28.825 --> 00:30:32.886
Its responses dictated
by an elaborate software

00:30:32.929 --> 00:30:34.396
written by a man.

00:30:34.431 --> 00:30:35.989
Its hardware built

00:30:36.032 --> 00:30:37.499
by a man.

00:30:37.534 --> 00:30:39.161
And now...

00:30:39.202 --> 00:30:41.693
And now a man will shut it off.

00:30:48.445 --> 00:30:50.310
Pinocchio is broken.

00:30:50.347 --> 00:30:52.838
Its strings have been cut.

00:31:05.896 --> 00:31:07.955
I request a recess.

00:31:08.031 --> 00:31:10.022
Granted.

00:31:24.079 --> 00:31:28.209
Do you mean his argument
was that good?

00:31:28.250 --> 00:31:31.344
Riker's presentation
was devastating.

00:31:31.387 --> 00:31:33.378
He almost convinced me.

00:31:33.422 --> 00:31:35.549
Well, you've got the
harder argument.

00:31:35.591 --> 00:31:38.219
By his own admission
Data is a machine.

00:31:38.260 --> 00:31:41.161
That's true.

00:31:41.196 --> 00:31:43.994
You're worried about what's
going to happen to him?

00:31:44.033 --> 00:31:49.198
Oh, I've had to send people
on far more dangerous missions.

00:31:49.238 --> 00:31:51.763
Well, then this should
work out fine.

00:31:51.807 --> 00:31:53.502
Maddox could get lucky

00:31:53.542 --> 00:31:56.340
and create a whole
army of Datas--

00:31:56.378 --> 00:31:57.845
all very valuable.

00:31:57.880 --> 00:31:59.347
Oh, yes, no doubt.

00:31:59.381 --> 00:32:02.373
He's proved his value to you.

00:32:04.820 --> 00:32:09.723
In ways that I cannot even begin
to calculate.

00:32:09.758 --> 00:32:14.957
And now he's about to be ruled
the property of Starfleet.

00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:17.965
That should increase his value.

00:32:21.136 --> 00:32:22.694
In what way?

00:32:22.738 --> 00:32:26.196
Well, consider that,
in the history of many worlds

00:32:26.241 --> 00:32:29.267
there have always been
disposable creatures.

00:32:29.311 --> 00:32:30.938
They do the dirty work.

00:32:30.979 --> 00:32:34.073
They do the work
that no one else wants to do

00:32:34.116 --> 00:32:37.176
because it's too difficult
or too hazardous.

00:32:37.219 --> 00:32:39.915
And an army of Datas,
all disposable...

00:32:39.955 --> 00:32:42.583
You don't have to think
about their welfare.

00:32:42.624 --> 00:32:44.785
You don't think
about how they feel.

00:32:44.827 --> 00:32:52.097
Whole generations
of disposable people.

00:32:52.134 --> 00:32:55.535
You're talking about slavery.

00:32:55.571 --> 00:33:00.804
Oh, I think
that's a little harsh.

00:33:00.843 --> 00:33:04.074
I don't think
that's a little harsh.

00:33:04.113 --> 00:33:06.411
I think that's the truth.

00:33:06.448 --> 00:33:10.043
But that's a truth
that we have obscured

00:33:10.085 --> 00:33:13.521
behind a comfortable,
easy euphemism--

00:33:13.555 --> 00:33:16.251
property.

00:33:16.291 --> 00:33:20.125
But that's not the issue
at all, is it?

00:33:28.904 --> 00:33:32.396
Commander Riker has dramatically
demonstrated to this court

00:33:32.440 --> 00:33:36.433
that Lieutenant Commander Data
is a machine.

00:33:36.478 --> 00:33:37.911
Do we deny that?

00:33:37.946 --> 00:33:40.813
No, because it is not relevant.

00:33:40.849 --> 00:33:45.980
We, too, are machines, just
machines of a different type.

00:33:46.054 --> 00:33:49.285
Commander Riker
has also reminded us

00:33:49.324 --> 00:33:52.725
that Lieutenant Commander
Data was created by a human.

00:33:52.761 --> 00:33:53.989
Do we deny that? No.

00:33:54.095 --> 00:33:57.121
Again, it is not relevant.

00:33:57.165 --> 00:33:59.531
Children are created

00:33:59.568 --> 00:34:03.561
from the building blocks
of their parents' DNA.

00:34:03.605 --> 00:34:08.941
Are they property?

00:34:09.044 --> 00:34:12.536
I call Lieutenant Commander
Data to the stand.

00:34:27.896 --> 00:34:29.693
What are these?

00:34:29.731 --> 00:34:31.198
My medals.

00:34:31.232 --> 00:34:32.494
Why do you pack them?

00:34:32.534 --> 00:34:34.627
What logical purpose
do they serve?

00:34:34.669 --> 00:34:36.864
I do not know, sir.

00:34:36.905 --> 00:34:38.634
I suppose none.

00:34:38.673 --> 00:34:40.800
I just wanted them.

00:34:40.842 --> 00:34:42.605
Is that vanity?

00:34:45.513 --> 00:34:47.140
And this?

00:34:47.182 --> 00:34:48.809
A gift from you, sir.

00:34:48.850 --> 00:34:50.715
You value it?

00:34:50.752 --> 00:34:51.912
Yes, sir.

00:34:51.953 --> 00:34:53.147
Why?

00:34:53.188 --> 00:34:56.248
It is a reminder
of friendship and service.

00:35:09.871 --> 00:35:11.839
And this?

00:35:11.873 --> 00:35:15.832
You have no other portraits
of your fellow crew members.

00:35:15.877 --> 00:35:17.071
Why this person?

00:35:17.112 --> 00:35:21.276
I would prefer not
to answer that question, sir.

00:35:21.316 --> 00:35:22.806
I gave my word.

00:35:22.851 --> 00:35:27.515
Under the circumstances,
I don't think Tasha would mind.

00:35:29.824 --> 00:35:31.917
She was special to me, sir.

00:35:31.960 --> 00:35:35.293
We were...

00:35:35.330 --> 00:35:37.230
intimate.

00:35:47.008 --> 00:35:48.566
Thank you, Commander.

00:35:48.610 --> 00:35:51.943
I have no further questions
for this witness.

00:35:51.980 --> 00:35:55.245
Commander Riker,
do you want to cross?

00:35:55.283 --> 00:35:57.683
I have no questions, Your Honor.

00:35:57.719 --> 00:35:58.811
Thank you.

00:35:58.853 --> 00:36:00.844
You may step down.

00:36:03.858 --> 00:36:07.157
I call to the stand
Commander Bruce Maddox

00:36:07.195 --> 00:36:09.356
as a hostile witness.

00:36:18.873 --> 00:36:21.774
Verify, Maddox, Bruce,
Commander.

00:36:21.810 --> 00:36:25.837
Current assignment:
Associate Chair of Robotics

00:36:25.880 --> 00:36:28.781
Daystrom Technological
lnstitute.

00:36:28.817 --> 00:36:29.784
Major papers...

00:36:29.818 --> 00:36:30.785
Yes, yes, yes.

00:36:30.819 --> 00:36:32.582
Suffice it to say
he's an expert.

00:36:32.620 --> 00:36:34.383
Commander, it is your contention

00:36:34.422 --> 00:36:37.391
that Lieutenant Commander Data
is not a sentient being

00:36:37.425 --> 00:36:40.451
and, therefore, not entitled
to all the rights reserved

00:36:40.495 --> 00:36:42.793
for all life-forms
within this Federation?

00:36:42.831 --> 00:36:44.958
Data is not sentient, no.

00:36:45.066 --> 00:36:46.966
Commander, would you
enlighten us?

00:36:47.068 --> 00:36:48.968
What is required
for sentience?

00:36:49.003 --> 00:36:54.134
Intelligence, self-awareness,
consciousness.

00:36:54.175 --> 00:36:57.474
Prove to the court
that I am sentient.

00:36:57.512 --> 00:36:58.604
This is absurd.

00:36:58.646 --> 00:37:00.807
We all know you're sentient.

00:37:00.849 --> 00:37:03.317
So I'm sentient,
but Commander Data is not?

00:37:03.351 --> 00:37:04.648
That's right.

00:37:04.686 --> 00:37:06.244
Uh-huh. Why?

00:37:06.287 --> 00:37:08.653
Why am I sentient?

00:37:08.690 --> 00:37:10.817
Well, you are self-aware.

00:37:10.859 --> 00:37:13.350
Ah, that's the second
of your criteria.

00:37:13.394 --> 00:37:15.919
Let's deal with the first,
intelligence.

00:37:15.997 --> 00:37:17.328
Is Commander Data intelligent?

00:37:17.365 --> 00:37:18.491
Yes.

00:37:18.533 --> 00:37:22.367
It has the ability
to learn and understand

00:37:22.403 --> 00:37:24.530
and to cope with new situations.

00:37:24.572 --> 00:37:25.937
Like this hearing.

00:37:26.040 --> 00:37:27.166
Yes.

00:37:27.208 --> 00:37:29.574
What about self-awareness?

00:37:29.611 --> 00:37:31.408
What does that mean?

00:37:31.446 --> 00:37:33.937
Why... why am I self-aware?

00:37:33.982 --> 00:37:37.941
Because you are conscious
of your existence and actions.

00:37:38.019 --> 00:37:41.045
You are aware of yourself
and your own ego.

00:37:41.089 --> 00:37:43.614
Commander Data,
what are you doing now?

00:37:43.658 --> 00:37:45.649
I am taking part
in a legal hearing

00:37:45.693 --> 00:37:47.684
to determine my rights
and status--

00:37:47.729 --> 00:37:49.629
am I a person or property?

00:37:49.664 --> 00:37:50.961
And what's at stake?

00:37:51.065 --> 00:37:52.896
My right to choose.

00:37:52.934 --> 00:37:54.959
Perhaps my very life.

00:37:55.036 --> 00:37:57.470
"My rights."

00:37:57.505 --> 00:37:59.200
"My status."

00:37:59.240 --> 00:38:02.505
"My right to choose."

00:38:02.544 --> 00:38:04.808
"My life."

00:38:04.846 --> 00:38:12.754
Well, he seems reasonably
self-aware to me, Commander.

00:38:16.157 --> 00:38:18.853
I'm waiting.

00:38:18.893 --> 00:38:23.193
This is exceedingly difficult.

00:38:23.231 --> 00:38:25.495
Do you like Commander Data?

00:38:25.533 --> 00:38:26.932
I...

00:38:27.034 --> 00:38:32.939
I don't know it well enough
to like or dislike it.

00:38:33.040 --> 00:38:34.337
But you admire him?

00:38:34.375 --> 00:38:35.842
Oh, yes.

00:38:35.877 --> 00:38:38.437
It's an extraordinary piece...

00:38:38.479 --> 00:38:39.741
Of engineering and programming.

00:38:39.781 --> 00:38:40.748
Yes, you have said that.

00:38:40.782 --> 00:38:42.272
Commander, you have
devoted your life

00:38:42.316 --> 00:38:43.943
to the study of cybernetics
in general?

00:38:43.985 --> 00:38:45.043
Yes.

00:38:45.086 --> 00:38:46.451
And Commander Data
in particular?

00:38:46.487 --> 00:38:47.454
Yes.

00:38:47.488 --> 00:38:48.955
And now you propose
to dismantle him?

00:38:49.023 --> 00:38:51.958
So that I can learn from it
and construct more.

00:38:52.026 --> 00:38:53.459
How many more?

00:38:53.494 --> 00:38:55.428
As many as are needed.

00:38:55.463 --> 00:38:58.899
Hundreds, thousands,
if necessary.

00:38:58.933 --> 00:39:00.833
There is no limit.

00:39:00.868 --> 00:39:04.804
A single Data

00:39:04.839 --> 00:39:06.807
and forgive me, Commander

00:39:06.841 --> 00:39:08.206
is a curiosity.

00:39:08.242 --> 00:39:10.642
A wonder even.

00:39:10.678 --> 00:39:14.114
But thousands of Datas--

00:39:14.148 --> 00:39:18.585
isn't that becoming a race?

00:39:18.619 --> 00:39:21.918
And won't we be judged
by how we treat

00:39:22.023 --> 00:39:23.183
that race?

00:39:23.224 --> 00:39:26.057
Now tell me, Commander,
what is Data?

00:39:26.093 --> 00:39:28.891
I don't understand.

00:39:28.930 --> 00:39:30.090
What is he?

00:39:30.131 --> 00:39:31.098
A machine.

00:39:31.132 --> 00:39:32.497
-ls he? Are you sure?
-Yes.

00:39:32.533 --> 00:39:35.161
You see, he's met two of your
three criteria for sentience.

00:39:35.203 --> 00:39:37.194
So, what if he meets the third,
consciousness

00:39:37.238 --> 00:39:38.466
in even the smallest degree?

00:39:38.506 --> 00:39:39.837
What is he then?
I don't know.

00:39:39.874 --> 00:39:44.106
Do you? Do you?

00:39:45.813 --> 00:39:47.804
Do you?

00:39:52.887 --> 00:39:57.415
Well, that's the question
you have to answer.

00:39:57.458 --> 00:39:59.688
Your Honor, the courtroom
is a crucible.

00:39:59.727 --> 00:40:01.558
In it, we burn away
irrelevancies

00:40:01.596 --> 00:40:03.757
until we are left
with a pure product--

00:40:03.798 --> 00:40:05.231
the truth-- for all time.

00:40:05.266 --> 00:40:08.099
Now, sooner or later, this man,
or others like him

00:40:08.135 --> 00:40:10.569
will succeed
in replicating Commander Data.

00:40:10.605 --> 00:40:12.971
Now, the decision
you reach here today

00:40:13.074 --> 00:40:15.201
will determine
how we will regard

00:40:15.243 --> 00:40:17.473
this creation of our genius.

00:40:17.511 --> 00:40:20.639
It will reveal the kind
of a people we are

00:40:20.681 --> 00:40:21.978
what he is destined to be.

00:40:22.083 --> 00:40:24.210
It will reach far beyond
this courtroom

00:40:24.252 --> 00:40:25.844
and this one android.

00:40:25.887 --> 00:40:29.414
It could significantly
redefine the boundaries

00:40:29.457 --> 00:40:31.948
of personal liberty and freedom.

00:40:31.993 --> 00:40:34.393
Expanding them for some

00:40:34.428 --> 00:40:38.626
savagely curtailing them
for others.

00:40:38.666 --> 00:40:42.102
Are you prepared to condemn him
and all who come after him

00:40:42.136 --> 00:40:43.694
to servitude and slavery?

00:40:46.140 --> 00:40:50.008
Your Honor, Starfleet was
founded to seek out new life.

00:40:50.044 --> 00:40:51.807
Well, there it sits.

00:40:54.382 --> 00:40:55.872
Waiting.

00:41:01.222 --> 00:41:03.850
You wanted a chance to make law.

00:41:03.891 --> 00:41:04.949
Well, here it is.

00:41:05.059 --> 00:41:06.458
Make it a good one.

00:41:17.838 --> 00:41:20.238
It sits there looking at me

00:41:20.274 --> 00:41:22.936
and I don't know what it is.

00:41:22.977 --> 00:41:26.435
This case has dealt
with metaphysics

00:41:26.480 --> 00:41:31.577
with questions best left
to saints and philosophers.

00:41:31.619 --> 00:41:36.750
I'm neither competent
nor qualified to answer those.

00:41:36.791 --> 00:41:39.817
But I've got to make a ruling

00:41:39.860 --> 00:41:43.819
to try to speak to the future.

00:41:43.864 --> 00:41:48.528
Is Data a machine? Yes.

00:41:48.569 --> 00:41:52.096
Is he the property of Starfleet?

00:41:52.139 --> 00:41:53.970
No.

00:41:54.008 --> 00:41:58.411
We have all been dancing around
the basic issue--

00:41:58.446 --> 00:42:01.244
does Data have a soul?

00:42:01.282 --> 00:42:03.944
I don't know that he has.

00:42:03.985 --> 00:42:06.180
I don't know that I have.

00:42:06.220 --> 00:42:09.485
But I have got
to give him the freedom

00:42:09.523 --> 00:42:12.390
to explore
that question himself.

00:42:12.426 --> 00:42:15.793
It is the ruling of this court

00:42:15.830 --> 00:42:20.824
that Lieutenant Commander Data
has the freedom to choose.

00:42:34.081 --> 00:42:37.881
I formally refuse
to undergo your procedure.

00:42:37.918 --> 00:42:41.513
I will cancel
that transfer order.

00:42:41.555 --> 00:42:43.819
Thank you.

00:42:43.858 --> 00:42:47.453
And, Commander,
continue your work.

00:42:47.495 --> 00:42:51.932
When you are ready,
I will still be here.

00:42:51.966 --> 00:42:54.833
I find some
of what you propose...

00:42:54.869 --> 00:42:56.632
intriguing.

00:43:04.045 --> 00:43:05.842
He's remarkable.

00:43:05.880 --> 00:43:08.542
You didn't call him "it."

00:43:18.225 --> 00:43:22.559
You see, sometimes it does work.

00:43:24.932 --> 00:43:25.694
Phillipa.

00:43:30.237 --> 00:43:31.795
Dinner?

00:43:31.839 --> 00:43:34.034
You buying?

00:43:48.355 --> 00:43:52.985
Sir, there is a celebration
on the holodeck.

00:43:53.027 --> 00:43:55.393
I have no right to be there.

00:43:55.429 --> 00:43:57.590
Because you failed in your task?

00:43:57.631 --> 00:43:58.825
No, God, no.

00:43:58.866 --> 00:44:00.993
I came that close to winning,
Data.

00:44:01.035 --> 00:44:02.332
Yes, sir.

00:44:02.369 --> 00:44:04.599
I almost cost you your life.

00:44:04.638 --> 00:44:08.267
Is it not true that had you
refused to prosecute

00:44:08.309 --> 00:44:12.473
Captain Louvois would have ruled
summarily against me?

00:44:12.513 --> 00:44:14.242
Yes.

00:44:14.281 --> 00:44:19.150
That action injured you
and saved me.

00:44:19.186 --> 00:44:22.053
I will not forget it.

00:44:24.492 --> 00:44:27.052
You're a wise man, my friend.

00:44:27.094 --> 00:44:28.527
Not yet, sir

00:44:28.562 --> 00:44:32.464
but, with your help,
I am learning.
